#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0552 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC structure=BDS. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), MCRIT1ML(Char). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | HIGH`. The mirror of scenario 1: the COMPANION MCRIT1ML is declared and the CONDITION variable MCRIT1MN is not, so the first conjunct `var_exists('MCRIT1MN')` is FALSE and the rule stays silent. This is the DISCRIMINATING direction test - it is the scenario that fails if the two operands are ever swapped. The rule still EXECUTES (expect=noViolation, not skipped) because `MCRITyML` matches MCRIT1ML and seeds the tuple y=1; MCRIT1MN is then synthesised as absent."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col MCRIT1ML type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | HIGH
